      "raw": "I have a dilemma. &nbsp;You see, FantasyLiterature.com is holding their [url=http://www.fantasyliterature.com/giveaway/thoughtful-thursday-our-annual-limerick-contest/]annual limerick contest[/url]. &nbsp;And as you&#39;ve probably gathered, I&#39;m rather fond of limmericks. &nbsp;On the other hand, of [url=http://www.fantasyliterature.com/giveaway/thoughtful-thursday-fantasy-limericks/]the[/url] [url=http://www.fantasyliterature.com/giveaway/thoughtful-thursday-fantasy-limericks-2/]three[/url] [url=http://www.fantasyliterature.com/giveaway/thoughtful-thursday-fantasy-limericks-3/]contests[/url] they&#39;ve held so far, I&#39;ve won two of them (I used to go by the username of Sir Read-a-Lot). &nbsp;So should sit back and let other people participate, or should I participate anyways? &nbsp;I don&#39;t care about the prize - I just like limericks.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n(Incidentally, if you like the look of the books in their [url=http://www.fantasyliterature.com/fanlit-stacks/]stacks[/url], they hold giveaways every Thursday, with rarely more than a dozen participants. &nbsp;I&#39;ve even won books by accident, just because I had a comment I wanted to make)\n",
